# Code owners for security-sensitive paths.
#
# Required review from a code owner is the INTENDED mitigation for the PR
# disposition merge gate's listener-coverage-narrowing and
# required-check-provenance gaps (see docs/development/reviewing.md): a
# candidate PR should not be able to merge a change under .github/workflows/
# -- including narrowing pr-disposition-review-trigger.yml's
# pull_request_review.types coverage, or authoring an unrelated workflow that
# mints its own check run named "disposition" -- without an independent owner
# approving that exact change.
#
# That protection is intended, NOT currently observed. "Require review from
# Code Owners" is already enabled on the `main` ruleset, yet changes under
# .github/ have merged with no native APPROVED review. Enabling the setting
# was therefore not the missing step, and this entry must not be relied on as
# an active independent-approval gate until the behavior is established and
# repaired. Open issue #313 owns that controlled verification and repair.
# CODEOWNERS alone does not enforce anything.
#
# This file also owns itself (and the rest of .github/), per GitHub's own
# guidance that protecting a repository fully against unauthorized changes
# requires defining an owner for CODEOWNERS in addition to the paths it
# protects: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# Without this, a PR could narrow or remove the /.github/workflows/ rule
# below in one change, then narrow the listener's trigger coverage or spoof
# the disposition check name in a later, no-longer-covered change.
/.github/ @alaiba

/.github/workflows/ @alaiba
